<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Which article should I read first?</h3>
<p>Start with failure modes if you are diagnosing a returned battery; start with plate and grid design if you are specifying a new product. Both paths link to the electrolyte and formation articles when you need the process detail.</p>
<h3>Why does grid alloy matter?</h3>
<p>The alloy sets the corrosion rate, water-loss behaviour and deep-cycle tolerance. A calcium alloy is not automatically better than antimony; it is better for low-maintenance float duty, while antimony is more forgiving in repeated deep cycling.</p>
